# Project: mes_pft — Cigarette Filter MES (Manufacturing Execution System)

## Stack
- Backend: FastAPI (`backend/app`), served by uvicorn.
- Database: PostgreSQL, migrations via Alembic (`backend/alembic/versions/`).
- Frontend: Flutter (tablet + web console); the web build is served by FastAPI at `/`.
- ERP: Odoo 18 Community via XML-RPC (`backend/app/services/odoo/`).

## Environments (dev vs production)
- **DEV MES server:** uvicorn on port **8001** (`uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8001`).
- **DEV Odoo server:** `http://127.0.0.1:8070` (dev database `test`). Never 8069 on dev.
- **Custom Odoo addons** live at `C:\Odoodev` (especially `mes_integration`). The dev
  Odoo config `C:\OdooDev\odoo-dev.conf` (port 8070, db `test`) loads them via
  `C:\OdooDev\odoo_my_addons` — the two paths resolve to the same files. May be read
  and edited for reference and development.
- **Addon changes** need more than a restart when the manifest version or data files
  change: run the module upgrade
  `odoo-bin -c C:\OdooDev\odoo-dev.conf -d test -u mes_integration --stop-after-init`
  (see `docs/odoo-integration.md`).
- **PRODUCTION MES:** installed at `C:\mes_system` (Windows task `MES_Server`). **Never edit
  production files directly** — changes go through dev first, then are pushed/copied via
  `scripts/update_server.ps1` (or the documented procedure).
- **PRODUCTION Odoo addons:** inside Program Files (Odoo server addons). **Never edit
  production Odoo addons** — develop in `C:\Odoodev` and deploy the tested addon.
- **Workflow:** implement → test on dev (MES 8001 + Odoo 8070) → push/copy to production.
  After each modification, restart the dev MES server and/or the dev Odoo server if needed
  (`uvicorn --reload` picks up backend Python changes, but Odoo addon changes require
  restarting the Odoo dev service).
- Dev smoke tests in `backend/scripts/` (e.g. `smoke_test_quarantine_release.py`) target the
  **DEV** Odoo (127.0.0.1:8070). Never run them against production.

## Releases / versioning
- The software version lives in TWO places and must be bumped together:
  `frontend/pubspec.yaml` (version name + build number) and
  `backend/app/version.py` (`SOFTWARE_VERSION`). Then rebuild the APK and the
  web console and copy the APK into `apk_releases/` for the auto-update flow.
- The backend also exposes a counts-based DATA version (`/api/version` ->
  `version` / `data_version`) - it changes when records change, not on releases.

## Roadmap
- Consult **ROADMAP.md** (repo root) for open questions, technical-debt backlog and decided
  items before starting a task. Update it whenever an item is resolved or a new gap is found.

## Key directories
- backend/app/models.py          — SQLAlchemy models (single source of truth)
- backend/app/v2_routes.py       — unified `/api/v2` routes (pure HTTP layer)
- backend/app/quality_stats.py   — pure statistics (no DB/framework imports; unit-tested)
- backend/app/services/          — station_watcher, shift_resolver, aggregation, odoo/*
- backend/alembic/versions/      — raw-SQL migrations, sequential IDs 0001, 0002, ...
- frontend/lib/core/             — hash navigation, app navigation, open_new_tab (web/stub conditional exports)
- frontend/lib/dashboard/        — 24-column dashboard grid engine
- frontend/lib/screens/web/      — web console screens

## Commands
- Run backend (dev):  cd backend && uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8001
- Run tests:    cd backend && python -m unittest discover -s tests -t .
- Migrate:      cd backend && .venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic upgrade head
- Build web:    cd frontend && flutter build web --release
- Docker:       docker compose --env-file .env up -d --build

## Invariants (do not violate)
1. Never commit secrets: `.env`, `*.jks`, keystores and tokens are gitignored. Use `.env.example` templates.
2. Odoo `odoo_*` columns are NULLABLE and linking is additive only — never delete or
   overwrite existing production data (17 materials, 44 POs, 150k+ measurements).
3. New DB schema goes through Alembic only (raw SQL in a new 000N migration).
   Do not add runtime ALTER TABLE (legacy migrate_db.py is frozen).
4. Frontend navigation is direct `setState` + `setHash` (which uses history.replaceState).
   Do NOT rely on a `hashchange` event listener — it is unreliable in this build.
5. `quality_stats.py` must stay pure (importable with no DB/env) so it remains unit-testable
   and reusable by the Odoo payload builder.
6. Web/non-web platform splits use conditional exports
   (`export 'stub.dart' if (dart.library.html) 'web.dart'`) — never import dart:html in non-web builds.
7. Dev/prod separation: never edit production MES files in `C:\mes_system` or production Odoo
   addons in Program Files directly. Change on dev first, test, then push/copy to production.

## Quality methodology (reference)
- Rod rejection: a value outside nominal ± 3×(nominal−limit) is rejected and excluded from all stats.
- SD is reported as sample SD (n−1); weight is per-rod but certified per 100 rods (report_scale=100).
- Statistics are computed per production run (MO), never pooled across MOs.
